[h1]Operation Artemis[/h1]

[b]Survival was only the beginning.[/b]

A notebook taken from a military infected. A coded broadcast. Someone called V. Follow the evidence across Knox County, uncover Operation Artemis, and find a way out of the Exclusion Zone.

[h2]FOLLOW THE SIGNAL[/h2]

Read the notebook, tune a military radio and listen. The investigation starts inside your survival run: documents, clues and locations gradually reveal your next objective.

[h2]UNRAVEL THE OPERATION[/h2]

Explore a deserted bunker, a clinic, a radio relay and a secret underground base. Recover evidence, restore power when needed and make sense of V’s trail. Taking the dossier is only the start of your escape.

[h2]GET OUT ALIVE[/h2]

An alarm can turn a quiet search into a desperate climb out of the laboratory. Then choose your exit: helicopter evacuation, the river and its ferryman, or the checkpoint. Each route has its own conditions and ending.

[h2]WHAT CHANGES YOUR RUN[/h2]

[list]
[*]An investigation built into the existing world, with readable documents and a journal that keeps your discoveries.
[*]Danger with a purpose: power, alarms, security access and a laboratory escape.
[*]Several exfiltration routes, a victory screen and epilogues tied to your exit.
[*]An optional sterilization countdown, plus sandbox settings for discovery, intensity and extraction timing.
[/list]

[h2]START YOUR INVESTIGATION[/h2]

Enable Operation Artemis and [url=https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=3811010882]Signal Smoke[/url]. Find the Artemis notebook on military infected and read it. Let the clues guide you; the first step does not require debug commands.

[h2]BUILD & LANGUAGES[/h2]

Project Zomboid 42.21. Core helicopter, ferryman and checkpoint routes tested in singleplayer. Multiplayer and optional integrations still need their own validation. Story text and voiced endings: French and English.

[h2]SUPPORT THE PROJECT[/h2]

Enjoy the scenario? A coffee helps fund the next stories and updates.

